 "title": "Why every extraordinary person is good at sales",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "Kunal Shah explains that extraordinary people are always great at sales because selling is required in many situations, from hiring to convincing investors and bosses. The creator highlights that while traditional careers like engineering and doctor are valued in India, learning sales is essential to survive in the next ten years.",
 "key_points": [
  "All people who do well in life are extraordinary at sales.",
  "Hiring someone requires you to be great at sales.",
  "Convincing an investor requires you to be great at sales.",
  "Selling a product requires you to be great at sales.",
  "Convincing your boss to do something requires you to be great at sales.",
  "In India, becoming an engineer or a doctor is still seen as a career path.",
  "Pursuing a career in sales is not considered a safe choice.",
  "Sales is a skill that needs to be learned at any cost to survive in the next ten years."
 ],
 "content": "Text on screen: Kunal Shah explained why every extraordinary person is good at sales. Instagram reel/post by Sanika Chandrakar. Caption: It’s a clip from @thethinkschool podcast. Thank me later! [sales insights, closing deals, selling, negotiations] #salestips #salesandmarketing #startupfounder. Transcript: All the people who do well in life are extraordinary at sales. Correct. You want to hire somebody, you have to be great at sales. You want to convince an investor, you have to be great at sales. You want to sell a product, you have to be great at sales. You want to convince your boss to do something, you have to be great at sales. In India, we still believe becoming an engineer or a doctor seems like a career path. But pursuing a career in sales is not a safe choice. But it's a high time that we realize sales is something that we need to learn at any cost to actually survive in next 10 years.",
